{"blocks":[{"l":"header","b":[0.13,0.0996,0.1917,0.1169],"t":"Test 2"},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1271,0.1423,0.4733,0.1629],"t":"PART 4 Questions 31–40"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1283,0.1776,0.3692,0.1971],"t":"Complete the notes below."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1292,0.2103,0.5096,0.2297],"t":"Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer."},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.2617,0.2557,0.7833,0.2798],"t":"Agricultural programme in Mozambique"},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1433,0.2851,0.49,0.3052],"t":"How the programme was organised"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1425,0.3178,0.7987,0.3538],"t":"It focused on a dry and arid region in Chicualacuala district, near the Limpopo River."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1425,0.3596,0.85,0.3803],"t":"People depended on the forest to provide charcoal as a source of income."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1442,0.3853,0.8929,0.4059],"t":"31 was seen as the main priority to ensure the supply of water."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1446,0.4121,0.7733,0.4477],"t":"Most of the work organised by farmers' associations was done by 32 ....."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1446,0.4545,0.7408,0.4739],"t":"• Fenced areas were created to keep animals away from crops."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1442,0.481,0.4221,0.4999],"t":"The programme provided"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1871,0.506,0.5062,0.5252],"t":"– 33 ___ for the fences"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1875,0.532,0.5367,0.5514],"t":"– 34 ..... for suitable crops"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1875,0.5591,0.3329,0.5779],"t":"— water pumps."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1454,0.5912,0.3871,0.6097],"t":"The farmers provided"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1862,0.6174,0.2708,0.6359],"t":"— labour"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1862,0.6427,0.6242,0.6613],"t":"— 35 ___ for the fences on their land."},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1458,0.6689,0.3629,0.6872],"t":"Further developments"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1446,0.6937,0.7608,0.729],"t":"- The marketing of produce was sometimes difficult due to lack of 36 ....."},{"l":"text","b":[0.145,0.7364,0.8292,0.7561],"t":"Training was therefore provided in methods of food 37"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1454,0.7614,0.8192,0.782],"t":"Farmers made special places where 38 could be kept."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1462,0.7879,0.7117,0.8077],"t":"Local people later suggested keeping 39 ....."},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1467,0.8138,0.4529,0.833],"t":"Evaluation and lessons learned"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1454,0.8392,0.8263,0.8595],"t":"• Agricultural production increased, improving incomes and food security."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1458,0.8648,0.8854,0.9025],"t":"- Enough time must be allowed, particularly for the 40 ..... phase of the programme."},{"l":"number","b":[0.1313,0.9184,0.1583,0.9337],"t":"36"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1917,0.914,0.4213,0.9364],"t":"→ p. 121 p. 105"}]}